{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Information.EulerCharacteristicOfHochschild","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Information.EulerCharacteristicOfHochschild","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Interval","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.NegOnePow","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.hhEuler_bring","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.hhEuler_bring","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/EulerCharacteristicOfHochschild.lean#L122-L125","doc":"**Bring's curve, `g = 4`: `−6`.** The `−6` of `lem:brings-euler-characteristic`\nis this alternating sum, not a trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.hhEuler_curve","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.hhEuler_curve","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/EulerCharacteristicOfHochschild.lean#L116-L120","doc":"**For a curve of genus `g` the Hochschild Euler characteristic is `2 − 2g`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.hhDim_curve_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.hhDim_curve_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/EulerCharacteristicOfHochschild.lean#L112-L114","doc":"`dim HH_{−1} = h^{1,0}`, read as `H^1(𝒪)`: `g`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.hhDim_curve_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.hhDim_curve_one","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/EulerCharacteristicOfHochschild.lean#L108-L110","doc":"`dim HH_1 = h^{0,1}(Ω¹) = h^{0,1}`, read as `H^0(Ω^1)`: `g`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.hhDim_curve_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.hhDim_curve_zero","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/EulerCharacteristicOfHochschild.lean#L104-L106","doc":"`dim HH_0 = h^{0,0} + h^{1,1} = 2`: the rank and the point class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.curveHodge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.curveHodge","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/EulerCharacteristicOfHochschild.lean#L96-L102","doc":"The Hodge numbers of a smooth projective curve of genus `g`:\n`h^{0,0} = h^{1,1} = 1` and `h^{1,0} = h^{0,1} = g` (Serre duality). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.hhEuler_eq_hodgeEuler","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.hhEuler_eq_hodgeEuler","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/EulerCharacteristicOfHochschild.lean#L72-L92","doc":"**The alternating sum over Hochschild homology is the Hodge Euler characteristic**\n(sorry-free). Re-index `Σ_n Σ_{j − i = n}` as `Σ_{i,j}` and apply `neg_one_zpow_sub`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.neg_one_zpow_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.neg_one_zpow_sub","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/EulerCharacteristicOfHochschild.lean#L64-L70","doc":"`(−1)^{j − i} = (−1)^{i + j}` in `ℤ`: the two exponents differ by `2i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.hodgeEuler","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.hodgeEuler","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/EulerCharacteristicOfHochschild.lean#L58-L62","doc":"The Hodge Euler characteristic `Σ_{i,j} (−1)^{i+j} h^{i,j}`. The Hodge\ndecomposition identifies it with `χ_eu(X)`; that identification is cited, not\nproved here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.hhEuler","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.hhEuler","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/EulerCharacteristicOfHochschild.lean#L53-L56","doc":"The Euler characteristic of Hochschild homology, `Σ_{n = −d}^{d} (−1)^n dim HH_n`.\nThe sign `(−1)^n` for `n : ℤ` is `Int.negOnePow n`, coerced to `ℤ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.hhDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.hhDim","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/EulerCharacteristicOfHochschild.lean#L48-L51","doc":"HKR at the level of dimensions: `dim HH_n = Σ_{j − i = n} h^{i,j}`, the sum over\nthe `(d+1) × (d+1)` Hodge square. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.HodgeNumbers","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.HodgeNumbers","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/EulerCharacteristicOfHochschild.lean#L44-L46","doc":"Hodge numbers `h i j = dim H^i(X, Ω^j)` of a `d`-dimensional variety, as a\nfunction on `ℕ × ℕ` (entries with `i > d` or `j > d` are never read). ","signatureChunk":0}]}